From 7e0f2a442f39348507eba8ad3ae6fce8a458263d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Dennis Klappe <dennisklappe@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 8 Sep 2026 14:19:40 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] Lift the licence gate on guest accounts

The guest account implementation ships in full in the AGPL server, only the
gates are licence-checked. Removes every one of them:

  server/channels/utils/license.go   GuestAccounts client props
  server/channels/api4/user.go       createUser guest-invitation token,
                                     login, getLoginType, magic-link mail,
                                     demoteUserToGuest
  server/channels/api4/team.go       inviteGuestsToChannels
  server/channels/api4/role.go       patching guest role permissions

Without the createUser and login hunks a guest could be invited but never
redeem the invite or sign in, which made the rest of the lift useless.

Guest accounts now follow GuestAccountsSettings.Enable alone.

See https://mattermore.dev/guest-accounts
---
 server/channels/api4/role.go      | 14 ++------------
 server/channels/api4/role_test.go | 10 +++++-----
